sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-anthrobots-06> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-06--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-06--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-anthrobots-06: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.40" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.399"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "needs-new-data" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.74"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Seeding density, diameter and motile fraction are all measured quantities, and the paper describes half, default and double density. Those curves remain with the authors. Without the replicate table, the significance and the non-linear shape cannot be recomputed from open data." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: At 15,000, 30,000 and 60,000 cells per millilitre, record final bot diameter and the day-by-day motile fraction. A significant, non-linear shift in both size and the motility time course would support seeding density as a control parameter; overlapping size distributions, or a strictly linear response, would refute the stated pattern." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Three-density size and motility curves are not deposited.", "Density also changes nutrient and oxygen competition, so it is not a pure morphological knob.", "Non-linearity is hard to establish from three points without the raw replicates." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-06--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of levin-2024-anthrobots-06 by Grok 4.7: 0.88" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
